Moseley's law relates the frequency 
u of characteristic X-rays emitted by an element to its atomic number Z by the relation: \sqrt{
u} = a(Z - b), where a and b are constants.
Statement I asserts that a plot of \sqrt{
u} against atomic mass is linear, which is false because the linear relationship holds specifically with atomic number Z, not atomic mass.
Statement II asserts that a plot of 
u against atomic number is a straight line, which is false because \sqrt{
u} (not 
u) is linearly proportional to Z.
Therefore, both Statement I and Statement II are false → (C)
